id: pm-5oj5
title: "Capability: Observability, telemetry & health"
description: "Improve observability: structured remediation, local telemetry analytics, validate --fix-hints, schema versioning"
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:observability","area:telemetry",backlog,living-map,pm-cli
created_at: "2026-05-31T19:42:12.693Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T02:27:14.985Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: Telemetry pipeline survives infra restarts without event loss; health and validate advisories carry actionable remediation hints; stats expose percentiles and error rates.
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Improve observability: structured remediation, local telemetry analytics, validate --fix-hints, schema versioning"
value: "Actionable, privacy-preserving diagnostics for agents and operators"
why_now: "Release gates and agent recovery depend on telemetry that distinguishes product defects, expected refusals, infrastructure faults, queue delivery, and recurrence; historical Sentry and pipeline incidents show that missing classification turns repaired defects into repeated release blockers."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: "Telemetry survives infrastructure restarts without loss, and every health or validate advisory names the action that clears it."
