comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-06-06T18:32:16.466Z",github-triage-subagent,"Observability/telemetry triage 2026-06-06: latest scheduled Nightly Validation run 27055539337 succeeded across Node 20/22/24/25 plus macOS/Windows matrix. Local node scripts/release/sentry-telemetry-gate.mjs --json --telemetry-mode best-effort --max-critical 0 --max-high 0 --max-telemetry-error-rate 10 --max-telemetry-missing-error-rows 0 returned ok=true: Sentry checked with 0 critical/high issues, 14 ignored expected CLI errors, telemetry finish_error_rate_pct 1.9, and failures_without_error_code_rows 0. First attempted mode 'warn' was rejected because supported values are off, best-effort, required."
  "2026-06-09T22:33:32.773Z",codex-active-pm-cycle-20260610,"2026-06-10 signal sync snapshot: GH alerts are clean (dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning all empty). Sentry org=unbrained project=pm-cli: unresolved issue list is dominated by expected command-error scenarios; recent TypeError clusters (PM-CLI-1G/1H) are currently resolved. Continue monitoring PM-CLI-1J tracker_not_initialized serialization events for UX clarity."
  "2026-09-13T10:18:11.182Z","harness:codex","Context-maintenance correction during PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1254: the charter contained an old fixed child count and a hand-maintained open-child list. Replaced that volatile snapshot with the canonical all-status parent query and typed graph. The prior text remains in immutable history; the capability remains open and implementation ownership is not retained for this metadata-only refresh."
  "2026-10-04T04:47:00.952Z","harness:codex","Live observability census 2026-10-04: required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero unresolved critical/high issues and zero telemetry failures missing an error code. Last-day telemetry query returned 6,228 finished actions, 61 failures (0.98%), and a current-day ingestion timestamp. Explicit queue flush drained pending records to zero with acknowledged delivery. Sentry issue query for unresolved lastSeen:-14d returned no rows; a fresh one-hour trace query also returned no rows. This proves recent action telemetry and clean issue inventory, not universal action completeness or recent Sentry trace visibility. Private raw operations output remains outside tracked files. Parent stays open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-04T07:44:07.302Z","harness:codex","Fresh reliability observation 2026-10-04T07:41Z: required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with critical=0, high=0 and a 14-day activity window. Collector report observed 6,566 finishes and 73 failures in the last day (1.11%). Current CLI flush drained one queued entry to zero and reported success. These observations establish recent event ingestion and bounded reliability, not complete tracing of every user action. Earlier one-hour and 24-hour Sentry trace queries returned no rows; trace completeness remains unverified."
  "2026-10-06T01:11:31.194Z","harness:codex","Fresh observability evidence 2026-10-06T01:08Z during pm-dba47 and pm-cql43 verification: Sentry unresolved query returned no issues and one-hour trace query returned no rows. The consent-preserving CLI flush drained one queued entry to zero with acknowledged success. Twenty current collector rows include real stats telemetry assurance changelog context history and get command starts/finishes. Most client/server timestamp deltas are subsecond; four get rows have negative deltas near minus1.5 to minus1.8seconds. These signed values cannot be claimed as physical ingestion latency without reconciling producer and collector clocks. Keep clock/trace interpretation as observation and existing capability followup; no trace completeness or universal action coverage is established. Private operational receipts remain ignored and no host addresses or credentials are added. Capability remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-10T04:17:07.857Z","harness:codex","Current 2026-10-10 release-delivery observation: required Sentry and telemetry gates pass with zero critical/high Sentry findings and zero missing telemetry failure-code rows. Backend queries observe recent command_start/command_finish ingestion, and consent-preserving flush acknowledged queued delivery. Both automatic project detection and explicit unbrained/pm-cli fresh 1-hour trace queries return complete empty populations after a real context command with supported full trace sampling. Trace freshness remains unverified; do not reinterpret clean issue inventory or local flush success as universal live tracing. Existing capability/history already owns this boundary, so no duplicate incident is created. Private raw receipts remain outside tracked files."
  "2026-10-10T18:51:21.168Z","harness:codex","Live recovery-delivery verification 2026-10-10: required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero critical/high unresolved findings and zero failures missing an error code. A fresh backend15-minute window observed180 command starts and180 finishes with current timestamps; this is aggregate correspondence, not universal action completeness. Flush acknowledged pending delivery to zero, and the subsequent status action legitimately queued its own event. Explicit unbrained/pm-cli fresh24-hour traces remain empty, including after a valid read with supported full sampling. Trace freshness remains unverified under this existing capability; no duplicate incident or synthetic production fault was introduced. Private receipts stay outside tracked files."
  "2026-10-10T19:31:14.567Z","harness:codex","Final pre-PR observability recheck: Sentry issue access and severity thresholds pass with zero current critical/high issues; required live telemetry has3.47percent finish error rate and zero failures missing an error code. A real stats CLI read with full trace sampling and an explicit successful SDK flush was followed by a fresh24-hour trace query returning no rows. Producer initialization/flush success does not prove hosted ingestion, so the existing recent-trace visibility acceptance remains unverified. Chrome Computer Use was retried on the existing CodeFactor tab, but the selected Chrome browser remains unavailable; no alternate browser automation was used."
  "2026-10-10T20:46:48.636Z","harness:codex","Fresh pushed-head operational verification 2026-10-10: required issue/telemetry gate passes with zero Sentry current critical/high/error issues, 2.9 percent finish error rate and zero failures missing an error code. A backend 15-minute sample has recent real action timestamps and 107 finishes; a separate session/command correspondence query observed 108 matched sessions, one start gap older than two minutes and one recent gap. This bounds the evidence and does not establish universal action completeness or its cause. Fresh 24-hour traces remain empty after previously verified producer initialization/flush. Continue using this existing observability lineage; no synthetic production fault or private event payload was published."
  "2026-10-10T20:51:37.982Z","harness:codex","The configured SDK default ingestion target was compared with the live authenticated unbrained/pm-cli project: they match, and this process has no environment DSN override. Empty fresh traces therefore are not explained by a mismatched target in this check; producer flush success still does not establish hosted trace ingestion. No Sentry settings, sampling defaults or paid service features were changed."
  "2026-10-10T22:53:31.635Z","harness:codex","Fresh final-remediation observability reads at 2026-10-10 22:49-22:52 UTC: a real stats action and explicit telemetry flush report enabled transport and a recent successful flush. The required Sentry/telemetry gate passes: authenticated unbrained/pm-cli has zero issues/critical/high in the 14-day window, finish-error rate 2.9 percent and zero failures lacking error codes. A separate private 15-minute session aggregate observes 99 matched sessions, zero mature start gaps and one recent start gap; a subsequent event-count query observes 101 starts, 99 finishes and 8 command errors, with its latest start at 22:52 UTC. These are separate query snapshots, not a universal completeness proof. The fresh 24-hour hosted trace list remains empty with no pagination; earlier verified DSN/project identity does not establish ingestion. Queue count remains three after flush because the flush command itself emits events; permanent drainage is not claimed. No trace-ingestion cause or universal action completeness is inferred, and this broader observability lineage remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-10T22:56:14.127Z","harness:codex","Additional private hash-only queue correspondence at 22:56 UTC: the queue was empty before a real flush action, then contained one newly generated row afterward, with zero unchanged rows and a successful flush timestamp. This directly demonstrates that an instrumented flush action can regenerate the queue; no event identifiers or payloads are published and no permanent-empty claim is made."
  "2026-10-11T02:27:14.985Z","harness:codex","PR #1436 b07c19d3853d1cc60a12e61d7cf7e6b4ce4d6d88 live observability receipt at 2026-10-11 02:00-02:01 UTC: Sentry 14-day issue gate has zero total/critical/high issues with access and threshold checks passing; required telemetry reports 2.9% finish-error rate and zero failures missing codes. Flush drained its one queued event and reported an empty queue at that instant. Read-only recent aggregates have 66 matched sessions, zero mature start gaps and one recent start gap, with latest real event at 02:01:25 UTC. Hosted fresh 24-hour trace query remains empty, so no hosted trace-visibility or universal-action-completeness claim is made; this broader epic remains open and unclaimed."
body: "## Charter\nLiving capability epic for observability: pm health checks, validate fix-hints, remediation registry, local telemetry stack (OTLP export, worker, Postgres/RabbitMQ/Grafana on the remote host), Sentry integration, and stats/percentiles.\n\n## Scope\n- In: health/validate/doctor advisory surfaces, remediation-registry completeness, telemetry capture levels + redaction, telemetry stats (percentiles/error-rate/agent-identity), Sentry gates in release flow.\n- Out: CI gates themselves (pm-u9d0), secrets handling policy (never write host IPs/tokens to tracked files — standing rule).\n\n## Live work and outcomes\nUse `pm list --all --parent pm-5oj5 --full` and the typed dependency graph for current child status, ownership, and outcomes. Each canonical child retains its implementation, incident, and verification evidence; historical counts and hand-maintained open-child lists are not a live status source."
